      "side": 1,
      "message": "There is a lot of common code between icm42607.c and icm426xx.c, where the only difference are the registers.\nWe had the same problem in the past with kionix sensors (see accel_kionix.c).\nOne way is to have a private macro V() set to 1 when compiling for icm42607.\n\nAssuming ICM426XX_GYRO_FS_MAX_VAL as been renamed ICM42605_GYRO_FS_MAX_VAL\n\nThen we can use register like\n#define ICM426XX_GYRO_FS_MAX_VAL(v) (ICM42605_GYRO_FS_MAX_VAL + v * (ICM42607_GYRO_FS_MAX_VAL - ICM42605_GYRO_FS_MAX_VAL)\n\nIn the common code, we would use register ICM426XX_GYRO_FS_MAX_VAL(V(s)).",
      "revId": "95387d8c2ea23cf305bb01be2a8dc74b8d850de0",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
